      "side": 1,
      "message": "Rather than directly using `c_void`, it\u0027s possible to create distinct types to represent these structures. That allows the Rust type checker to distinguish between these types. With `type` aliases like this it would otherwise treat them interchangeably.\n\nSee\n- https://doc.rust-lang.org/nomicon/ffi.html#representing-opaque-structs\n- https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/ffi/enum.c_void.html",
      "range": {
