    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f4d7abcc_9bc249a0",
        "filename": "media/ndk/mediacodec-rs-ndk/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 432,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291337
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-19T23:03:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The [documentation](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/av/media/ndk/include/media/NdkMediaFormat.h;l\u003d65;drc\u003d5af7fb15ce95b8dd9ea87a982290242a05406002) of `AMediaFormat_toString` writes\n\n\u003e The returned string is owned by the format, and remains valid until the next call to toString, or until the format is deleted.\n\nBecause `MediaFormat` is marked as `Sync`, it would technically be possible for two threads to have an execution with the following ordering:\n\nA: str_1 \u003d AMediaFormat_toString(format)\nB: str_2 \u003d AMediaFormat_toString(format)\nA: c_str \u003d CStr::from_ptr(str_1)\n\nThis is a race because `str_1` is no longer valid after the second call to `AMediaFormat_toString`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 426,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 432,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "a3a74b4a7778837c5bea9cccd1ccb56f6880de5f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6084c1b1_d6c8dbe5",
        "filename": "media/ndk/mediacodec-rs-ndk/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 450,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291337
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-19T23:03:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A safer type to use would be `Box\u003cPin\u003cSender\u003cAsyncMessage\u003e\u003e\u003e`. `Pin` is the Rust way to describe \"an instance that must stay in the same location in memory.\"\n\nSee\n\n- https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/pin/struct.Pin.html#pinning-a-value-inside-a-box\n- https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/pin/",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 447,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 450,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "a3a74b4a7778837c5bea9cccd1ccb56f6880de5f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cfe74489_9bc32b47",
        "filename": "media/ndk/mediacodec-rs-ndk/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 460,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291337
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-19T23:03:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: \"portable across thread boundaries\" is the meaning of `Send`, while `Sync` means \"multiple threads can call the `\u0026self` methods concurrently.\"",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 459,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 460,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "a3a74b4a7778837c5bea9cccd1ccb56f6880de5f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "03116c60_4d4ae542",
        "filename": "media/ndk/mediacodec-rs-ndk/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 576,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291337
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-19T23:03:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here and in `get_output_buffer`, this needs to guarantee not only that the memory is valid at the time that this function is called, but also that it is valid for the lifetime of the type that is returned.\n\nWithout explicitly setting a lifetime here, `\u0026mut [u8]` will default to having the same lifetime as `\u0026self`, which may extend beyond the real lifetime of that memory (based on some interaction with `queue_input_buffer` and `release_output_buffer`?)\n\nRepresenting the real lifetime probably involves creating a new type to wrap the buffer that can have its own lifetime and be consumed by `queue_input_buffer` or `release_output_buffer`.\n\nA faster way to get out of this problem at the expense of performance is to create a copy, returning a `Vec\u003cu8\u003e` instead of a `\u0026mut [u8]`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 575,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 576,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "a3a74b4a7778837c5bea9cccd1ccb56f6880de5f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b176e010_4879d28e",
        "filename": "media/ndk/mediacodec-rs-ndk/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 576,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291337
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-19T23:07:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually realized a copy may work for `get_output_buffer` but probably not for this function, since it\u0027s returning a mutable reference probably intending the caller to write data to it.\n\nA more appropriate strategy for `get_input_buffer` specifically could be to accept data from the caller and copy it into the memory returned by `AMediaCodec_getInputBuffer`.\n\nIn both cases the \"simple\" way is to avoid the `AMediaCodec_getInputBuffer` / `AMediaCodec_getOutputBuffer` pointer \"escaping\" by providing a higher level interaction, while the more complex way is to create a new type that represents the true lifetime of the underlying pointer type.",
      "parentUuid": "03116c60_4d4ae542",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 575,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 576,
        "endChar": 38
      },
